&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;actively pro-inclusive and anti-racist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; across our community, clients and creations  &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;OLIVER,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;a part of the Brandtech Group, is an equal opportunity employer committed to creating an inclusive working environment where all employees are encouraged to reach their full potential, and individual differences are valued and respected. All applicants shall be considered for employment without regard to race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, neurodivergence, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by local laws. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; OLIVER has set ambitious environmental goals around sustainability, with science-based emissions reduction targets. Collectively, we work towards our mission, embedding sustainability into every department and through every stage of the project lifecycle.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Amplitude is the leading AI analytics platform, helping over 4,700 customers—including Atlassian, Burger King, NBCUniversal, and Square—build better products and digital experiences. With powerful AI Agents embedded across our platform, teams can analyze, test, and optimize user experiences faster than ever. Ranked #1 across multiple categories in G2’s Winter 2026 Report, Amplitude is the best-in-class solution for product, data, and marketing teams. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;http://amplitude.com&quot;&gt;amplitude.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an organization, we deliver for our customers by living our values. We operate from a place of humility, take ownership of problems and successes, approach challenges with a growth mindset, and put our customers at the center of everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Amplitude’s Commitment to Diversity Equity &amp;amp; Inclusion (DEI): &lt;/strong&gt;Amplitude believes that diversity enables the creation of better products, improves the ability to solve complex problems, and drives more powerful solutions. We strive to create an environment of inclusion—one focused on psychological safety, empathy, and human connection—that will allow employees of all backgrounds to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Amplitude is building the operating system for digital product innovation—and our Deal Desk team sits right at the centre of how we monetise that vision.This team partners deeply with Sales, Finance, Legal, and Revenue Accounting to structure smart, scalable deals that accelerate growth without introducing risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Deal Desk Manager, you’ll act as player/coach with a view to progress into a people manager role to lead our International Deal Desk team. You will act as the senior strategic advisor on our most complex international deals and operate with real autonomy — given clear guardrails, but trusted to make the call. You’ll help shape deal strategy, guide pricing and contract decisions, and bring clarity to ambiguity—all while keeping the business moving fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Senior Deal Desk Manager, you will:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Amplitude’s International Deal Desk team — supporting with hiring, coaching, and setting the bar for how the team partners with Sales, Finance, and Legal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own deal strategy for complex, high-risk international deals, advising Sales leadership on pricing, packaging, contract terms, and negotiation strategy — including setting precedent where policy doesn’t yet exist&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and approve complex non-standard transactions end-to-end, ensuring approvals align with revenue recognition, legal, and operational policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the connective tissue across Sales, Legal, Finance, RevOps, and Accounting, resolving disagreements and driving alignment across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale the Quote to Order process — codifying best practices and driving adoption of AI tools and automation across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be a great addition to the team if:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re genuinely comfortable operating in ambiguity as the senior decision-maker on the ground.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in a fast-paced environment with high-stakes deals that require creative thinking and sound judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build trust with Sales by being a valued partner—creative, collaborative, and solution-oriented—while still holding the line when it matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re energised by cross-functional collaboration and know how to drive alignment across strong personalities and competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have sharp judgment on risk and detail, balanced with knowing when a rule should flex and when it shouldn’t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a clear, thoughtful communicator with strong critical thinking skills and a constant drive to improve systems, processes, and how teams work together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At a minimum, you need to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in Deal Desk, Sales Operations, or a similar deal strategy role in a SaaS or subscription-based business, including complex, enterprise-scale transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of operating autonomously and making independent decisions, ideally in an international, remote, or distributed-team setting removed from the core of a leadership team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or evolving deal desk policy, pricing frameworks, or approval processes — not just operating within them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Legal and Finance on non-standard terms and approvals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Salesforce (CPQ experience strongly preferred) and comfort working with data and complex deal scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with channel selling model and transacting through cloud marketplaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;By applying for this job, you acknowledge that Amplitude processes your personal data in accordance with the &lt;a href=&quot;https://amplitude.com/job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Amplitude Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Staying Safe - Protect Yourself From Recruitment Fraud&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;We are aware of individuals and entities fraudulently representing themselves as Amplitude recruiters and/or hiring managers. Amplitude will never ask for financial information or payment, or for personal information such as bank account number or social security number during the job application or interview process. Any emails from the Amplitude recruiting team will come from an @&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;http://amplitude.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://amplitude.com&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;amplitude.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;email address. You can learn more about how to protect yourself from these types of fraud by referring to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://consumer.ftc.gov/consumer-alerts/2023/05/scammers-are-hijacking-job-ads-heres-how-spot-fakes&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://consumer.ftc.gov/consumer-alerts/2023/05/scammers-are-hijacking-job-ads-heres-how-spot-fakes&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;this article&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;. Please exercise caution and cease communications if something feels suspicious about your interactions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;QRT is a global quantitative and systematic investment manager, operating across all liquid asset classes. We are a data- and technology-driven organization applying scientific methods to investing. Our collaborative culture and focus on innovation enable us to solve complex challenges and deliver high-quality returns for our investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Treasury Desk manages QRT’s funding, collateral, cash balances and counterparty relationships. The Treasury Analytics Team builds the data infrastructure and tools that support financing decisions and help the firm deploy capital efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your future role within QRT&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced Quantitative Technologist to support our Treasury Analytics Team by developing analytical tools that enhance trading decisions across asset classes. The role is expected to involve the following activities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Design, develop and maintain production-grade analytical and trading applications for the Treasury Desk.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Build value-add analytics to optimise Treasury trading decisions across asset classes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Work closely with Treasury stakeholders to understand trading requirements and translate them into scalable technical solutions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Onboard and integrate new datasets to support trade idea generation, financing analysis and decision-making.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Design software architectures and data solutions that integrate the Treasury data ecosystem with the broader QRT technology platform.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Enhance existing analytics platforms by addressing performance bottlenecks, reducing read latency and improving system scalability.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Develop new technological capabilities, including real-time analytics and AI-enabled agent workflows.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Contribute across all stages of the software development lifecycle, from solution design and implementation through to testing, deployment and production support.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Continuously improve the Treasury Desk’s engineering standards, technical architecture and development practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your present skillset:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • 3–5 years’ experience working as a Quantitative Developer, Quantitative Technologist or in a similar role&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Strong quantitative skills and a solid understanding of financial markets&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Good knowledge of fixed income products and markets&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Demonstrable experience designing, building and supporting production-grade software systems&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Strong understanding of software architecture, object-oriented design and common software design patterns&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Strong database knowledge, including indexing, partitioning, caching and query optimisation&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Comfortable contributing across all stages of the software development lifecycle&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Demonstrable ability to communicate and collaborate effectively with technical and business stakeholders&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Desirable to have experience or a willingness to learn in the following areas:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Statistics, quantitative modelling or financial analytics&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Cloud-native technologies, including AWS, Docker, Kubernetes and infrastructure automation&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Real-time data processing and analytics&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Financial data infrastructure and the integration of complex data ecosystems&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Modern AI-assisted software development tools&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; • Treasury, financing, collateral or liquidity management systems&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;QRT is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome diversity as essential to our success. QRT empowers employees to work openly and respectfully to achieve collective success. In addition to professional achievement, we are offering initiatives and programs to enable employees achieve a healthy work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re Capital on Tap 👋&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;💳 Capital on Tap started because small businesses were underserved. Big banks were slow, their products weren&#39;t fit for purpose, and small business owners often couldn&#39;t access what they needed. We set out to fix that.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Today we&#39;re a financial platform - not just a credit card company. We offer a best-in-class business credit card, SME-focused spend management platform, a savings product that hit £1 billion in funds within its first year, and a growing suite of tools and financial products that make running a small business easier.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;1,000+ employees, £20bn in annual card spend, 200,000+ customers, 17,000+ Trustpilot reviews averaging 4.7 stars, and we&#39;re profitable. We’ve done a pretty good job so far, but we’re just getting started!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;📍 London | 🏢 3 days in office&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product at Capital on Tap 🚀 Our Product team sits at the heart of everything we build. We move fast, work closely with engineering, and obsess over outcomes for our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking a Product Designer to join our centralised team of three, contributing across product areas as our web and mobile apps continue to grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This hybrid role will touch the journeys customers use to run their businesses, while helping shape our design system. Expect variety: one week you&#39;re defining a component, the next you&#39;re designing a feature or supporting an acquisition campaign. Work here isn&#39;t handed over as a spec to execute; you&#39;re expected to think from first principles and bring a point of view.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Where the time goes: roughly 70% UX and Product, 20% UI and Visual Design, 10% Marketing and Growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;d be designing the tools small business owners use to make real financial decisions, and work where getting it right shapes someone&#39;s day. It&#39;s also a good place to grow. A small team means more ownership sooner and more of the whole job: you&#39;re in the prioritisation conversations, not just receiving their output, and you work across the business rather than in one corner of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for someone early in their design career, keen to grow into owning features end to end with support from senior designers along the way&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;re curious, proactive, and comfortable asking questions rather than waiting for a brief.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-5 years in product or UX design, ideally with some exposure to a design system (Figma and/or code).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio showing solid UX fundamentals (problem definition, interaction, usability, accessibility) alongside a good eye for visual polish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in Figma and working knowledge of modern design and prototyping tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You go and find out.&lt;/strong&gt; You take unknowns to whoever holds the answer, support, engineering, ops, data, rather than escalating or guessing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You define design by what it needs to do&lt;/strong&gt;, then apply the right elements and patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You build from the kit.&lt;/strong&gt; You reach for existing solutions before inventing, and can tell when they genuinely don&#39;t cover the case rather than forcing a bad fit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Great to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to design ops, design tooling, or AI-assisted workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with design-to-production workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work in a scaling product org with multiple teams or product surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview Process 🤝&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🤝 First stage: 30 minute intro and values call with Talent Partner (Video call)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🤝 Second stage: 45 minute Technical Chat with Lead Product Designer (Virtual/in person)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🤝 Final stage: 60 minute presentation interview with 2-3 members of the team + 30 minute interview with Head of Department&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Other Info&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;👍Check out our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.capitalontap.com/en/blog/posts/acing-your-interviews-with-capital-on-tap/&quot;&gt;‘Top Tips’ for interviewing.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;✔️Keep updated on new job opportunities by following us on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/capital-on-tap&quot;&gt;Linkedin&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;📧Email &lt;a ---------- if you have any questions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excited to work here? Apply!&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: verdana, geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;If you’d like to progress your career within our fast growing, profitable fintech then click apply and we will aim to get back to you within 3 working days (during busy periods this could take up to 5 working days.)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; color: #662d91;&quot;&gt;Teamwork makes the stream work.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Roku is changing how the world watches TV&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku is the #1 TV streaming platform in the U.S., Canada, and Mexico, and we&#39;ve set our sights on powering every television in the world. Roku pioneered streaming to the TV. Our mission is to be the TV streaming platform that connects the entire TV ecosystem. We connect consumers to the content they love, enable content publishers to build and monetize large audiences, and provide advertisers unique capabilities to engage consumers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From your first day at Roku, you&#39;ll make a valuable - and valued - contribution. We&#39;re a fast-growing public company where no one is a bystander. We offer you the opportunity to delight millions of TV streamers around the world while gaining meaningful experience across a variety of disciplines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mt-6 mb-2 font-semibold text-xl&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;heading-3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;font-semibold&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;What is the role?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-200 my-2.5 last:mb-0 first:mt-0 &quot;&gt;Roku is seeking a Senior Counsel, Employment and Labor to join its Legal team, providing strategic guidance on a broad range of employment, labor, benefits, and related matters across the UK, EMEA, and global operations. In this role, you will partner closely with People Business Partners, People Shared Services, Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits, and other cross-functional teams to translate complex legal requirements into clear, actionable advice. You will draft and negotiate employment agreements, settlement agreements, and other key documents, while managing employment-related claims, litigation, and outside counsel relationships. You will monitor evolving employment legislation and proactively drive compliance strategies and risk mitigation across the organization. This position requires an entrepreneurial mindset and the ability to work independently in a fast-paced, innovative environment, balancing multiple priorities and stakeholders. The ideal candidate brings deep expertise in UK employment and labor law, with exposure to additional EMEA or international jurisdictions, and a commitment to practical, business-oriented legal counsel.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mt-6 mb-2 font-semibold text-xl&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;heading-3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;font-semibold&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;How will I use AI at Roku?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-200 my-2.5 last:mb-0 first:mt-0 &quot;&gt;At Roku, AI agents and AI-enabled tools handle a growing share of first-draft, repetitive, analytical, and execution-heavy work across the company. Our people lead those systems; setting direction, providing context, exercising judgment, and stepping in when work needs correction or deeper thinking. If you are excited about working this way, we want to talk to you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-200 my-2.5 last:mb-0 first:mt-0 &quot;&gt;You can describe specific examples where you used AI tools, agents, or workflow automation to move faster, raise quality, or scale your impact. You frame problems well, guide AI-assisted work, verify results, and ramp quickly in unfamiliar domains. Above all, you bring curiosity, adaptability, good judgment, and a willingness to learn new ways of working. At Roku, we&#39;re embracing AI as a powerful tool to amplify human creativity, accelerate innovation, and deliver better results for our customers. Across teams, we&#39;re exploring how AI can enhance our work—and we&#39;re only looking for people who are curious, adaptable, and excited to grow alongside these technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mt-6 mb-2 font-semibold text-xl&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;heading-3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;font-semibold&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;What are the responsibilities of the role?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;list-inside list-disc whitespace-normal [li_&amp;amp;]:pl-6&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;unordered-list&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;py-1 [&amp;amp;&gt;p]:inline&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Advise People Business Partners, People Shared Services, Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits, and other partner teams on employment matters including hiring, performance management, grievances, disciplinary actions, investigations, redundancies, reorganizations, and wage and hour compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;py-1 [&amp;amp;&gt;p]:inline&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Provide counsel on agency worker and contractor engagement, reasonable accommodations, flexible work requests, leaves of absence, employee privacy, data security, benefits, TUPE transfers, and works councils&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;py-1 [&amp;amp;&gt;p]:inline&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Support the development and maintenance of a global employment and labor framework, including handbooks, policies, and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;py-1 [&amp;amp;&gt;p]:inline&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Research and monitor employment legislation and legal developments, proactively implementing compliance and risk-mitigation strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;py-1 [&amp;amp;&gt;p]:inline&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Review and advise on contractual agreements with third-party service providers, vendors, and staffing agencies, as well as internal practices for engaging contingent workers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;py-1 [&amp;amp;&gt;p]:inline&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Draft and negotiate employment agreements, performance and disciplinary notices, settlement agreements, and other employment-related documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;py-1 [&amp;amp;&gt;p]:inline&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Advise on complex and sensitive employment matters, facilitating pre-dispute resolution and positioning the organization for potential employment litigation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;py-1 [&amp;amp;&gt;p]:inline&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Manage employment-related claims and litigation globally, including overseeing outside counsel, responding to complaints and settlement demands, and negotiating resolutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;py-1 [&amp;amp;&gt;p]:inline&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Assist with preparing, reviewing, and implementing employee training programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;py-1 [&amp;amp;&gt;p]:inline&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Support additional legal projects and initiatives as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
